WEBVTT

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.040
What did they say at the Ministry?

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.440
Liu or Santos?

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.120
Officially, the Ministry
takes no position.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.440
Unofficially, smart
money's on Santos.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.640
Although anyone would
be better than Vogel.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.920
Anyone?

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.640
I don't believe he's
on the ballot, Kama.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.800
He also happens to be a fugitive.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.240
Is there a difference?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.680
(rumbling)

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.960
Spinning! Always with the spinning.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:50.880
(Newt) Jacob.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.560
Welcome. You brilliant man.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.880
Sorry.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.480
I was absolutely sure that
Professor Hicks would convince
you.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.840
Yeah.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.720
You know me, pal. I can't pass
up a good Portkey. (chuckles)

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.200
Mr. Scamander.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.680
Professor Hicks.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.840
-At long last. -At long last.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.160
So, Professor Hicks and I, we've
corresponded for many years,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.440
but we've never actually met.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.840
So, her book on advanced charm
casting is a must-read.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.200
Newt is far too kind.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.160
Fantastic Beasts is required
reading for all my fifth years.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.600
Now, let me make some
introductions.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.920
So, this is, um, Bunty Broadacre,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.960
my indispensable assistant
for the past seven years.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.480
Eight. Years.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.800
And 164 days.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.320
-(Lally) Hmm. -As you
can see, indispensable.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.560
And this is...

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.520
Yusuf Kama.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.840
Pleasure.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.360
And you, obviously, already
made Jacob's acquaintance.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.800
(Theseus clears throat) Newt.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.520
So... So, this is my
brother, Theseus,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.960
and, um, he works for the Ministry.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.080
Actually, head of the
British Auror Office.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.480
Ah! Well, I'll have to ensure my
wand registration's up-to-date.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.000
Yes.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.000
Although, strictly speaking, that
doesn't fall within my purview.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.040
(Newt mumbles)

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.400
(puts suitcase down)

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.280
(gasps) Oh.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.360
(sighs)

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.040
(Newt) All right then.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.560
Well, I imagine that you're all

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.400
wondering why you
find yourselves here.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.040
And in anticipation of that,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.520
Dumbledore asked that
I convey a message.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.600
So, Grindelwald has the ability
to see snatches of the future.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.240
So, we have to assume

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.760
that he'll be able to anticipate
what we do before we do it.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.800
So, if we hope to defeat
him and to save our world,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.480
to save your world, Jacob,

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.000
then our best hope is to confuse
him.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.520
Uh...

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.600
'Scuse me.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.040
I'm sorry. How do you confuse a
guy that can see the future?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.760
Countersight.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.400
(Newt) Exactly.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.200
The best plan being no plan.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.880
Or, many overlapping plans.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.120
Thus, confusion.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.120
It's working on me right now.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.760
In fact, Dumbledore asked that
I give you something, Jacob.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.120
(Pick squeaks)

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.160
It's snakewood.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.840
It's, uh, somewhat rare.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.840
Are you kiddin' me right now?

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:27.960
Is this thing real?

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.280
Yes.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.360
Well, it doesn't have a
core, so sort of, but yes.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.240
It's sorta real?

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.040
More importantly, where we're
going, you'll need it.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.520
Now, there's something for you
too, I think, Theseus. Um...

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.840
-(rustling) -Teddy,
please let go now.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.120
-Teddy, please let go. -(sighs)

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.400
No. Teddy, will you behave?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.040
This is Theseus's...

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.560
(chitters, sniffing)

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.000
Um, that's...

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.600
Well, of course.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.640
Now everything makes sense.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.280
Um, Lally, I believe you were
given some reading material?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.400
You know what they say.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.120
A book can take you around
the world and back,

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.000
all you have to do is open it.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.120
She ain't kiddin'.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.520
(Newt) Yes, uh, Bunty, um...

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.560
that's for you.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.560
I was told it was for your eyes
only.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.440
(Bunty) Oh.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.400
(gasps)

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.440
Oh.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.840
And, Kama.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.880
I have what I need.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.600
What about Tina? Uh, is Tina
coming?

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.200
Tina's not available.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.400
Um...

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.720
Tina's been promoted, she's
very, very busy from...

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:49.800
well, from what I understand.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:53.400
Tina's been made head of
the American Auror Office.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.840
-(Jacob) Oh. -We know
each other well.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.560
She's quite a remarkable woman.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.160
She is.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.040
So, this is the team
that's gonna take down

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.600
the most dangerous wizard we've
faced in over a century.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.520
A magizoologist, his
indispensable assistant,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:07.800
a schoolteacher,

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.800
a wizard descended from a very
old French family, and...

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:11.840
(pops lips)

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:15.440
(inhales sharply) ...a Muggle
baker with his fake wand.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.200
Hey, we got you too, pal,

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.720
and his wand works.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.520
(Theseus scoffs)

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.360
Who wouldn't like our chances?

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.680
(cackles)

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.880
Oh. Uh... (clears throat)

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.320
-(sighs) -(train horn toots)

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.320
(dramatic music playing)

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:38.960
(brakes squeal)

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.800
(announcer speaking German on PA)

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:51.840
You're all right, little one.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.280
(train stops)

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.720
Berlin. (sighs)

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.040
Wonderful.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.160
Kama...

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.320
stay safe.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.960
(suspenseful music playing)

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.240
I must be going too now, Newt.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.120
No one can know everything...

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.000
not even you.

